experiment: staircase
  instrument        staircase   trial seed 0000000001357068   1214 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `travelsweep` found the shipped bar blind to target
                    distance past ~0.6 log units. `absbar` changes the BAR.
                    This changes the TARGET -- which is the axis the animal
                    protocol actually uses.
  the protocol      Tumer & Brainard step the pitch threshold each morning
                    rather than setting it far and waiting. The bird is never
                    asked for a jump it cannot straddle, and our invariance
                    holds only while the creature never crosses its target.
  the arms          jump:  target at 0.89 from trial 0, the current protocol.
                    stair: 0.15 -> 0.89 over the first half, then HELD, so the
                    late third that is scored sits at the same final target
                    in both arms. Matched marginal for each.
  the ramp          a fixed SCHEDULE on trial count, reading nothing about
                    the creature, so no oracle enters the arm.
  what would null   if the ceiling is the larynx rather than the protocol,
                    arriving gradually reaches the same place as arriving at
                    once and `stair` matches `jump`. That revives
                    `ceiling-is-an-exponent`, so this is worth running either
                    way. 36 seeds.

